 negative credit balance, you may see `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{})}),` errors, including for free models. Adding credits to put your balance above zero allows you to use those models again.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Per-key credit limits`}),`, an optional spending cap configured on an individual API key. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_reset`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_remaining`}),` fields in the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` response above describe this cap and how much of it remains.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`In-flight spending budget`}),`, a cap on the estimated token cost of the paid requests you have running or recently completed, relative to your balance. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#in-flight-spending-budget`,children:`In-flight spending budget`}),` below.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`in-flight-spending-budget`,children:`In-flight spending budget`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`OpenRouter charges a request when it finishes, so many requests running at the same time could commit more than your balance covers before any of them settles. To prevent that, OpenRouter estimates each paid request’s token cost up front, at the endpoint’s prices: the input tokens, plus the completion tokens allowed by `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`max_tokens`}),` up to a fixed per-request cap (the cap is used when `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`max_tokens`}),` is not set). Only token prices are estimated; per-request fees, plugin charges, and image pricing are not part of the estimate, so a request whose cost has no token component is not held. The estimate is held against your account while the request runs. When the request completes or fails, the hold is replaced by the request’s actual cost for a short settlement window, and then released.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The total that can be held at once is your in-flight spending budget: a fraction of your current credit balance, up to a fixed ceiling. A request whose estimated cost does not fit alongside your running and recently completed requests is rejected with `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{})}),` before it reaches a provider, even though your balance is positive. The error’s `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`metadata`}),` says which case you hit:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"reason\": \"in_flight_budget_exhausted\"`}),` with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"limit_source\": \"openrouter_in_flight_budget\"`}),`: your running and recently completed requests already fill the budget. This is transient and can occur with no request still running, while recent costs are settling. The response includes a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Retry-After`}),` header; wait for it and retry.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"reason\": \"weight_exceeds_budget\"`}),` with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"limit_source\": \"openrouter_credits\"`}),`: this single request’s estimated cost is larger than your whole budget, so retrying will not help. Lower `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`max_tokens`}),` or the prompt size, or add credits.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Every `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{})}),` whose `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`metadata`}),` carries `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_source`}),` also carries `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remedy_hint`}),`, a one-line human-readable next step for that source. It is meant for people reading logs; branch on `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_source`}),`, not on the hint text.`]}),`